	(text "1. Bare 1.5 mm ENIG pads on the bottom side, without paste or a fitted part; they are not in the BOM.\n2. Each pad sits in its probe row on the 2.54 mm grid, beside the row signals, for a short return loop.\n3. Pos counts along the row from its silkscreen label (west to east in top view), as on sheet 10 (Signal and programming probe access).\n4. The POWER and SWD row GND pads (TP6, TP40) are drawn with their rows on sheet 10 (Signal and programming probe access)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.88 138.43 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "719a9836-7609-5d61-b187-7f1c46c98cb0")
	)
